From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:18:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkvdec: vdpu381-vp9: keep the count table cacheable

After each frame that refreshes its frame context, rkvdec_vp9_done()
reads the symbol counts written by the decoder back and runs the VP9
backward probability adaptation on the CPU. The next frame of the
stream cannot be started before that is done, so this time is lost for
the hardware.

The count table was allocated with dma_alloc_coherent(), which is an
uncached mapping on RK3588, and v4l2_vp9_adapt_coef_probs() and
v4l2_vp9_adapt_noncoef_probs() read it one 32-bit counter at a time
through pointers into it. With the decoder interrupt handled on a
Cortex-A55 (the default IRQ affinity), the adaptation took ~430 us per
frame, ~7% of the decode time of a 3840x2160 frame (5.8 ms).

Allocate the table with dma_alloc_noncoherent() instead, write it back
before each decode and invalidate it before reading the counts. The
done handler goes from 437 us to 81 us per frame. Measured with
GStreamer v4l2slvp9dec into fakevideosink on an Orange Pi 5:

                           before        after
  3840x2160 8-bit          148 fps       156 fps
  3840x2160 8-bit, 2x      276 fps       286 fps
  3840x2160 10-bit         124 fps       130 fps
  3840x2160 10-bit, 2x     225 fps       238 fps
  1920x1080 8-bit          455 fps       538 fps

The decoded output is bit-identical.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c      | 24 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c
index 0f797e7012aa..c22b48d7b0bc 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
  * code from rkvdec_vp9_run() followed by rkvdec_vp9_done().
  */
 
+#include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/vmalloc.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-mem2mem.h>
@@ -539,6 +540,10 @@ static void config_registers(struct rkvdec_ctx *ctx,
 	if (intra_only)
 		memset(vp9_ctx->count_tbl.cpu, 0, vp9_ctx->count_tbl.size);
 
+	/* Write back the CPU's view of the count table before the decoder updates it. */
+	dma_sync_single_for_device(ctx->dev->main_core->dev, vp9_ctx->count_tbl.dma,
+				   vp9_ctx->count_tbl.size, DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
+
 	/*
 	 * Two segmentation maps are used in turn: the hardware reads the
 	 * segment IDs left by the previous frames from segidlast and writes
@@ -867,6 +872,10 @@ static void rkvdec_vp9_done(struct rkvdec_ctx *ctx,
 		if (frame_is_intra)
 			copy_tx_and_skip(probs, tx_skip);
 
+		/* make the symbol counts written by the decoder visible to the CPU */
+		dma_sync_single_for_cpu(ctx->dev->main_core->dev, vp9_ctx->count_tbl.dma,
+					vp9_ctx->count_tbl.size, DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
+
 		counts = frame_is_intra ? &vp9_ctx->intra_cnts : &vp9_ctx->inter_cnts;
 		v4l2_vp9_adapt_coef_probs(probs, counts,
 					  !vp9_ctx->last.valid ||
@@ -1021,8 +1030,14 @@ static int rkvdec_vp9_start(struct rkvdec_ctx *ctx)
 	vp9_ctx->priv_tbl.size = sizeof(*priv_tbl);
 	vp9_ctx->priv_tbl.cpu = priv_tbl;
 
-	count_tbl = dma_alloc_coherent(rkvdec->main_core->dev, RKVDEC_VP9_COUNT_SIZE,
-				       &vp9_ctx->count_tbl.dma, GFP_KERNEL);
+	/*
+	 * The CPU reads every symbol count back for the backward adaptation,
+	 * one 32-bit word at a time, so keep the table cacheable and
+	 * maintain it explicitly instead of using an uncached mapping.
+	 */
+	count_tbl = dma_alloc_noncoherent(rkvdec->main_core->dev, RKVDEC_VP9_COUNT_SIZE,
+					  &vp9_ctx->count_tbl.dma, DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL,
+					  GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!count_tbl) {
 		ret = -ENOMEM;
 		goto err_free_priv_tbl;
@@ -1048,8 +1063,9 @@ static void rkvdec_vp9_stop(struct rkvdec_ctx *ctx)
 	struct rkvdec_vp9_ctx *vp9_ctx = ctx->priv;
 	struct rkvdec_dev *rkvdec = ctx->dev;
 
-	dma_free_coherent(rkvdec->main_core->dev, vp9_ctx->count_tbl.size,
-			  vp9_ctx->count_tbl.cpu, vp9_ctx->count_tbl.dma);
+	dma_free_noncoherent(rkvdec->main_core->dev, vp9_ctx->count_tbl.size,
+			     vp9_ctx->count_tbl.cpu, vp9_ctx->count_tbl.dma,
+			     DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
 
 	dma_free_coherent(rkvdec->main_core->dev, vp9_ctx->priv_tbl.size,
 			  vp9_ctx->priv_tbl.cpu, vp9_ctx->priv_tbl.dma);
